    "narrative": "The **Austin Waves** offense hinges on a marquee matchup today, as **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (82.08) stands as our clear anchor. With a projected 0.376 xwOBA and a favorable matchup against the left-handed Rod\u00f3n, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** is positioned to exploit a significant platoon edge, provided his lineup slot remains at #2 as anticipated. We are also bullish on our exposure to the Severino matchup; both **Nolan Schanuel** (64.29) and **Josh Lowe** (64.94) benefit from the pitcher's elevated 4.60 xERA, which effectively boosts their base projections into strong starting territory despite the uncertainty of their official lineup spots.\n\nManaging our scarcity in the Stolen Base category remains a constant challenge, forcing us to lean into the efficiency of **Nasim Nunez** (51.41). While his spot in the #8 hole suppresses his overall score, his elite sprint speed makes him a necessary asset despite the tough defensive matchup against a high-caliber catcher. The most difficult bench decision today involved weighing **Dominic Smith** (53.57) against potential depth options; ultimately, the +7% platoon boost against Alcantara secured his spot, as he remains the superior high-floor play compared to our limited available reserves. \n\nWe are monitoring the weather and confirmed lineups closely for **Nolan Schanuel** and **Josh Lowe**; should either fall out of the top half of the order, their efficiency scores will regress toward the marginal range. Meanwhile, we continue to stash high-ceiling assets like **Kyle Tucker**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Andy Pages** during their scheduled off-days, while holding **Luis Robert Jr.** on the IL. With the rest of our roster\u2014including **Jackson Merrill**, **Jordan Westburg**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Drake Baldwin**, **Jorge Polanco**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Josh Jung**, **Coby Mayo**, **Miguel Vargas**, **Brady House**, **Sam Antonacci**, and **Gage Workman**\u2014in various stages of development or rotation, our current daily focus remains on squeezing maximum value out of **Liam Hicks** (54.43) to capitalize on the 4.20 xERA of Strider.",
